  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Herbertenolide may interact with CD276 antigen through a series of molecular targets. The drug is known to target Neuropilin-2, which in turn is a target of 3,4,5-Trimethoxycinnamic acid, (Z)-, and finally, this compound targets CD276 antigen. Similarly, Herbertenolide also targets Neuropilin-2, and another compound, Chondrosterin A, also targets CD276 antigen. These findings indicate that Herbertenolide may exert its biological effects through a pathway involving Neuropilin-2 and ultimately CD276 antigen. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where Herbertenolide acts as a modulator of the Neuropilin-2 signaling cascade, which is linked to CD276 antigen. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction between Herbertenolide and CD276 antigen.",
